-When the runtime bus drops a patch at its pending-delivery limit, every live domain receives a cursor invalidation on the same ordered lane after the queued backlog. Recovery reads the domain's authoritative snapshot, not the last published payload. A connection's outbound queue drops its oldest frames, never the connection, and each receiver answers the resulting gap with the ordinary resnapshot, with no reconnect or polling timer.
